From: MahanHD <mahanheidari2003@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: amami: mux the ADSP's sensor bus before it starts

The ADSP's first run failed on every boot. With the sensor registry's
accelerometer configuration it raised an exception about 50 ms after the
registry exchange; without it, it ran on but never found the
accelerometer. Either way the sensors came up only after a restart, and
on some boots not at all.

The sensors sit on BLSP2 QUP6 (GPIO 87/88), which the ADSP drives. The
bootloader leaves those pins as GPIO outputs driven low, and the ADSP
switches them to the I2C function only at its first transfer, so the
first sensor it probed always failed: swapping the accelerometer and
gyroscope slots in the registry moved the failure to the gyroscope.
Muxing the pins by hand before the start brought all four sensors up on
the first run, with no fault.

Give the ADSP node the bus's default pin state, so the pins are muxed
when the remoteproc probes, before the first start.

---
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8974-sony-xperia-rhine-amami.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8974-sony-xperia-rhine-amami.dts
@@ -997,3 +997,17 @@
 		/delete-property/ touchscreen-inverted-x;
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * The sensors hang off the ADSP on BLSP2 QUP6 (GPIO 87/88, "i2c_bus 12" in the
+ * sensor registry), and the bootloader leaves those pins as GPIO outputs driven
+ * low. The ADSP muxes them itself only at its first transfer, so whichever
+ * sensor it probed first failed on every cold start: the accelerometer went
+ * missing, or with the registry data of 0007 the ADSP faulted, and the sensors
+ * came up only after its restart. Mux them before it starts.
+ * blsp2_i2c6 itself stays disabled: the bus belongs to the ADSP.
+ */
+&remoteproc_adsp {
+	pinctrl-0 = <&blsp2_i2c6_default>;
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+};
